  "conclusion": "corresponds",
  "rationale": "RawStep.local delegates one Shared Unpacking step and preserves the active frame destination/callers. call has member, result-shape, pre-evaluation freshness, EvalArgs and length premises; it pushes a callee with destination d and retains the updated caller with its original destination d0. return evaluates and delivers using the callee destination, removes that frame and resumes the caller with its own destination. exit requires exactly one frame, empty statements, absent result and absent destination. Step has only the collect constructor, wrapping every raw transition; no intermediate expression-evaluation collection is possible. These four raw rules and the collection wrapper match the displayed mathematics. The pending-value discussion concerns atomic evaluation, not a proved stack realization invariant. Extension re-review: the exact authored unit and prior selected declarations/tests are unchanged from the previously reviewed packet. The added Destructor namespace and its explicitly stronger frame-exit/GC theorems do not change this earlier layer or its stated assumptions; reviewed the added source and updated repository scope separately. This is a differential author review, not a new independent assessment.",
